;; spec:   stdlib §4.4 (row iterate: an infinite source), §2.7 (three printers), §14 D7 of the tranche 2 plan (no Show for an endless source)
;; expect: reject
;; error:  no implementation of Show for (Iterate
;; roots:  ../../lib support
;; covers: print-str
;; An `Iterate` prints forever, as Clojure's `(println (iterate inc 0))` does, so the library gives it no
;; `Show`, and a compile error names the type: the program cannot print the whole of an endless source
;; by mistake. D7 of the plan is **Proposed (plan recommendation, owner not yet confirmed)**: no instance
;; of `Show`, `Debug` or `ToStr` for `Iterate`, `Repeat` and `Cycle` until `*print-length*` exists
;; (tranche 5). A bounded view prints (`(take 3 (iterate inc 0))` is an `LSeq`, case 2972). The error text
;; is the checker's, `no implementation of Show for (Iterate i64)`; the case keeps the type's name and
;; leaves its parameters out of the expected text.
(ns main)

(defun main () -> i64 (str-len (print-str (iterate inc 0))))
